    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0193" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.6363/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Southard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-20T14:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:52 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s instruction of August 29<anchor n="42" xml:id="d91-f1"
                    /> matter of Standard Oil Co. Permission for prospecting has been referred from
                    London to Jerusalem for recommendation. This Government has permitted meetings
                    informally to discuss it and assure me that it is being now returned to London
                    with favorable recommendation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
